  "label": "The woman is mapped as the 'me' in the text",
  "description": "The text 'If he's marrying me then why's he fucking a goat' explicitly refers to a female subject ('me') who is the victim of betrayal. The visual material shows a woman with an exaggerated expression of shock and disbelief, which is mapped onto this textual 'me'. The woman's emotional state and physical posture (hands on head, open mouth) are used to visually represent the shock and outrage implied by the text, making her the embodied representation of 'me' in the meme's narrative.",
